						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13447#msg13447"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13447#msg13447">Re: You know that EQ ended, right?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #32 on:</b> December 29, 2004, 03:05:13 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13445#msg13445">Quote from: umbrella on December 29, 2004, 02:32:26 pm</a></div><div class="quote">play eq all you want, wow blows away any other mmorpg on the market, and i am a die hard coh fanboy<br /></div>Great, I&#039;m happy for you.&nbsp; Have fun.&nbsp; The fact is that I&#039;m having fun playing EQ.&nbsp; I don&#039;t see a reason for me to leave the game for &quot;more fun&quot; somewhere else.&nbsp; I don&#039;t see a need to pay another 50 bucks for a new game, plus monthly fees, when I&#039;m enjoying the game that I currently play.&nbsp; I certainly don&#039;t have time to play both, and my EQ account is already paid for til May or June.&nbsp; If I wasn&#039;t having fun, I&#039;d leave, but since I am leaving would seem to be counterproductive.&nbsp; Plus, my friends are here, not in WoW, and I wouldn&#039;t have as much fun playing a new game without them.&nbsp; Maybe you have fun leaping from game to game (didn&#039;t CoH come out like 6 months ago?) but I don&#039;t.<br /><br />Plus, playing EQ I don&#039;t have to put up with the &quot;fanboys&quot; such as yourself.&nbsp; The friends and guildies I group with are mature and friendly, and rarely use phrases like &quot;rancid dogshit&quot; and &quot;die in the face&quot;.&nbsp; From what I&#039;ve heard, there are alot of &quot;in the face&quot; Diablo kiddies playing WoW.&nbsp; 
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
