							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							There&#039;s griefers in every game. There&#039;s still a fair number of fanboi&#039;s in EQ atm too.<br /><br />EQ is fun as long as you have a big group of people to keep moving forward, and the cannibalistic methods continue to operate, IE where the higher guilds are able to feed off the lower ones, and that the lower ones are continually able to recruit/train the new players.<br /><br />What&#039;s been happening, is there are far far fewer smaller guilds for the larger ones to feed off of. Unless server sonsolidations occur soonish, the pattern of guilds collapsing due to reduced players coming into the game, and the inability to continue to raid new content will destroy them all.<br /><br />The guilds with the highest turn over rates will suffer the most, or at least the fastest. Right now with a few guilds, including FoT having hit hard times, there are extra players available.<br /><br />2-3 months down the road, I doubt Rodcet will be able to consistently support any raiding guild of any quality, due to so many new games being on the market. Coupled with SoE&#039;s inability to listen to thier players, it&#039;s really evident that SoE is it&#039;s own worst enemy.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" /><a href="http://www.wowrankings.com/viewb.htm?name=Kinladar&amp;s_id=38" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/sig-kinladar-wow.jpg" alt="" border="0" /></a><br /><a href="http://www.chaoticdiscord.org" target="_blank">Chaotic Discord</a> found in {World of Warcraft}<br />Guild Leader of Fires of Time (Retired)
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg13450"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=522" title="View the profile of Self Destruction">Self Destruction</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 40<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v425/Undead13/Sharingan.gif" width="65" height="65" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								Sharingan!<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=522"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13450#msg13450"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/smiley.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13450#msg13450">Re: You know that EQ ended, right?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #34 on:</b> December 29, 2004, 05:13:28 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							&quot;EQ is fun as long as you have a big group of people to keep moving forward, and the cannibalistic methods continue to operate, IE where the higher guilds are able to feed off the lower ones, and that the lower ones are continually able to recruit/train the new players.&quot;<br /><br />You&#039;re looking at the situation based on what you like to do in the game and making it sound like it&#039;s the only reason to play. High end, hard core raiding is not the only thing to do in EverQuest. In fact, not even the majority play EQ this way. While it is a very important aspect, you do nothing but give a negative appearance to the game in it&#039;s entirety if you perpetuate this sky is falling attitude just because the way the (vocal) minority&#039;s game has been affected.<br /><br />I still think it&#039;s silly at least on Rodcet to make it sound like the high end is collapsing when there are still plenty of people on the server who are talented, well-geared and capable enough to still do this content. The cause of the decline may be new games coming out, but if the people who are left can&#039;t pick up the pieces and continute (even if it means mergers, recruiting and backflagging) then it&#039;s their own fault. The numbers are there...it&#039;s up to those guilds to make it work.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" /><img src="http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v425/Undead13/Virsig1.png" alt="" border="0" /><br /><br /><span style="font-family: arial;"><a href="http://www.magelo.com/eq_view_profile.html?num=859121" target="_blank"><font size="4">Fateseer Virulence</font></a></span><br /><span style="font-family: times;"><font size="3"><b>the Plague 70 Prophet</b><br /></font></span>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg13452"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=356" title="View the profile of Shado">Shado</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Hill Giant<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 193<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://espn-att.starwave.com/i/teamlogos/mlb/med/trans/bos.gif" width="65" height="65" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								hush u<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=356"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:jcroft412@yahoo.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13452#msg13452"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13452#msg13452">Re: You know that EQ ended, right?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #35 on:</b> December 29, 2004, 07:03:00 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I didn&#039;t really read this entire thread, but I would like to point out that is the recent mass of people quitting, wasn&#039;t just for a new game. I personally haven&#039;t let myself get wrapped up in any new game. I and a few other of my personal friends had quit because the game itself was going downhill, and watching it do that I saw tons of people get so emotional (including myself) over petty little things, the game for alot, again including myself had turned into a life, I finally had enough of getting so angry irl over the game. I&#039;m not trying to sound preachy or anything, just letting people know thats the reason myself and some others quit. It was a great game, a great escape but eventually you have to outgrow these hours on end on a video game.<br /><br />ANother things that makes me boggle is the thurst for &#039;&#039;drama&#039;&#039; over a video game, I took part of fueling the fires of these &#039;&#039;dramas&#039;&#039; over the years, and searching for some post about them. It&#039;s pretty ridiculous that so many people wanna hear about people on this game getting that pissed off over it, Like I said, I let EQ consume me for far to long.<br /><br />I recently considered coming back, because a certain fucker keeps buggin me too, but decided against it. FOr those reasons mostly..
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
