	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg13455"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=748" title="View the profile of Iniquitous">Iniquitous</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 17<br />
								<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=748"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13455#msg13455"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13455#msg13455">Re: You know that EQ ended, right?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #37 on:</b> December 29, 2004, 07:21:51 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I wouldn&#039;t say the sky is falling, but only because I don&#039;t think the death of EQ1 is the end of the world.&nbsp; It will be increasingly difficult to convince new players to play EQ1 when other games are clearly superior.&nbsp; People can argue that &quot;superior&quot; is relative to the player, but it doesn&#039;t really hold water when the players really do shun EQ1 for EQ2, WoW, Guild Wars, or (someday) Vanguard.&nbsp; People will look at the games they have to choose from and will easily see that EQ1 is a generation behind.&nbsp; New players -will- stop coming eventually.&nbsp; I make no prediction on when it will finally be too much loss for the system to bear.<br /><br />I&#039;m not trying to get anyone to play any game.&nbsp; However, EQ1&#039;s population will continue to decline.&nbsp; Less new players, combined with an inevitable retirement of existing players (no one plays forever), means a continually diminishing player base.&nbsp; It would be naive to expect it to last forever.&nbsp; Railing against the inevitable won&#039;t make it not happen.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg13456"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=522" title="View the profile of Self Destruction">Self Destruction</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 40<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v425/Undead13/Sharingan.gif" width="65" height="65" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								Sharingan!<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=522"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13456#msg13456"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13456#msg13456">Re: You know that EQ ended, right?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #38 on:</b> December 29, 2004, 09:59:07 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							&quot;Railing against the inevitable won&#039;t make it not happen&quot;<br /><br />And who&#039;s doing that? I don&#039;t recall seeing anyone in this thread claim (much less rail) that EQ will never end. Of course it will. My posts at least only deal with the near future of the game.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
