								My Avatar can beat up your avatar!<br />
								<br />
								
								<a href="http://members.msn.com/kinladar@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/msntalk.gif" alt="kinladar@hotmail.com" border="0" /></a>
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=1"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org" title="http://www.rodcetnife.org" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/www_sm.gif" alt="WWW" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:truman@thewavz.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13461#msg13461"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13461#msg13461">Re: You know that EQ ended, right?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #41 on:</b> December 30, 2004, 08:03:25 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I would no doubt guess some are, but the vast majority are just excited about something new, and interesting.<br /><br />Early adopter of anything are generally looked at with a skeptical eye in the begining, be it a new game, new technology, or what have you. There will always be a group of people who feel that what they have done in the past is good enough for them.<br /><br />That&#039;s fine, nothing wrong with that at all.<br /><br />There are certainly some flaws in WoW as well, but to state that nothing is wrong in the EQ world, and blindly adhere to that stance despite very obvious problems, is kinda short sighted.<br /><br />Biggest flaw in WoW yet is prolly customer service, since they did not expect any where near the flood of people they have now, they are under manned in the GM department, and getting replies has taken some time.<br /><br />There&#039;s a few bugged quests too, have reported them.<br /><br />I would have liked to see Battlegrounds, Hero Classes, and some of the other content put into place from the begining, but I get the general impression that Vivendi wanted the game released before christmas to get the holidays sales, and that sorta bugs me. Time will tell if this becomes a common pattern.<br /><br />And yes, you can still have fun in EQ, if you enjoy mindless grinds to get the runes, and other things that might get you a little recognition.<br /><br />But ho much fun is the game to play knowing that to see the best items, you will have to deal with raiding every single night, that it becomes more work than fun to get those items consistently, and that depending on what target you are doing the returns just don&#039;t match the efforts when you have 40-50 people there, each with a dozen slots, and you get 2 loots.<br /><br />Everyone&#039;s been on the have not side of the fence often enough, when you&#039;d like those great items, but you simply don&#039;t have the time to get them.<br /><br />For the efforts of a good 5 man group in WoW, you can get epic level items, that make people go wow (pun intended!) and of course there will be raid zones, but not needing nearly the numbers that an EQ raid needed.<br /><br />Alternatively, there will be epic level drops from the Battlegrounds as well, and such.<br /><br />There are so many avenues in WoW to advance all aspects of your characters versus EQ, and much more fun than grinding for hours to get a few AA skill points, it&#039;s just much better designed from the ground up.<br /><br />And yes this is my opinion, and as such, you are free to disagree with it, but disagree after you have seen both sides of the story, because to blindly sit there, and talk about a game you have never played, is sorta ignorant.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
