								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13462#msg13462">Re: You know that EQ ended, right?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #42 on:</b> December 30, 2004, 10:34:39 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13461#msg13461">Quote from: Kinladar on December 30, 2004, 08:03:25 am</a></div><div class="quote">disagree after you have seen both sides of the story, because to blindly sit there, and talk about a game you have never played, is sorta ignorant.<br /></div><br />Not sure who you&#039;re talking about here.&nbsp; The people I see posting like Virulence and Givins aren&#039;t posting about what&#039;s good or bad in WoW, they&#039;re talking about what they enjoy in EQ.&nbsp; And that subject - what <b>these particular people</b> enjoy in EQ, is something that they are experts on and that you know little about.&nbsp; <br /><br />Contrary to Gonaiel&#039;s post, 90% of everquest players are not &quot;high end raiders&quot;.&nbsp; People that spend all their time acquiring phat lewtz and raiding anguish/tac&#039;vi or whatever don&#039;t get the chance to see all the &quot;little people&quot; running around having fun.&nbsp; There are plenty of guilds raiding elementals, or lower, and lots more small guilds who aren&#039;t raiders at all.&nbsp; Not to mention the people who are lower levels (gasp) or are unguilded.&nbsp; <br /><br />Most of the items I get are from small groups and quests, and small (30ish people) raids.&nbsp; There are other ways to play Everquest without it being &quot;like a job&quot;, it&#039;s just that people have missed those in their pursuit of uberness.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
